\f0\b\fs18 \cf0 the princeton puzzle / 2025 / ink print on foam core board and wall-mounted installation
\f1\b0 \
\
Princeton\'92s campus, unlike universities with cohesive stylistic identities, is a heterogeneous architectural palimpsest where Gothic towers, Gehry\'92s parametric curves, and other eras coexist in dialogue. This layered, evolving environment\'97one reason I chose to study here\'97inspires my installation, which draws on Buster Keaton\'92s \'93anarchitectural\'94 play with space to reframe the campus not as static form but as a system of latent possibilities. By abstracting arches, thresholds, courtyards, and visual corridors, I highlight how buildings across time are unified less by style than by shared social functions of movement and gathering. Suspended components reconfigure these motifs into a flexible \'93ground,\'94 inviting viewers to see Princeton\'92s architecture not as backdrop but as an active agent shaping circulation, community, and new forms of belonging.}